      "id": 1,
      "text": "Simpson was named after pioneer William Simpson, a War of 1812 veteran who built one of the county's first taverns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/simpson_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village moved to its current spot when the Illinois Central Railroad arrived around 1887, sparking growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/simpson_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1888 Simpson incorporated, marking its transition from frontier settlement to formal village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/simpson_illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The surrounding Bay Creek watershed, part of the Ohio River system, covers 46% forested land, shaping local ecology.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
